1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,569
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,571 --> 00:00:03,016
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,238 --> 00:00:05,100
(Episode 70)

4
00:00:15,145 --> 00:00:17,056
I came to pay my respects to Ji Ni's dad.

5
00:00:17,484 --> 00:00:18,484
Mom.

6
00:00:21,931 --> 00:00:24,922
What are you doing here?
I told you to get lost!

7
00:00:24,924 --> 00:00:26,321
Mom, stop!

8
00:00:26,322 --> 00:00:29,235
I said no! I can't let her go!

9
00:00:31,558 --> 00:00:33,554
What's wrong with you two?

10
00:00:35,089 --> 00:00:37,318
What do you expect me to do?

11
00:00:38,525 --> 00:00:39,733
I'll treat her well, Mother.

12
00:00:40,072 --> 00:00:41,346
Please give me a chance.

13
00:00:41,398 --> 00:00:43,717
Mom, I'm not the same Ji Ni I used to be.

14
00:00:43,719 --> 00:00:46,106
I'll do better. I won't upset you.

15
00:00:48,372 --> 00:00:49,535
Please trust me.

16
00:00:55,125 --> 00:00:56,417
What are you going to do?

17
00:00:56,563 --> 00:00:57,831
She's your mom!

18
00:00:58,158 --> 00:00:59,921
Unless you're willing
to cut ties with her!

19
00:01:00,825 --> 00:01:04,598
Your dad kept going back
to his family home too. You saw that!

20
00:01:05,092 --> 00:01:07,678
The bond between parent
and child never breaks!

21
00:01:07,792 --> 00:01:09,612
My dad said he'll support me.

22
00:01:09,614 --> 00:01:10,614
I'm not cutting ties with them.

23
00:01:11,425 --> 00:01:13,592
I can do this, Mother. Don't worry.

24
00:01:15,478 --> 00:01:17,282
I'll make sure Ji Ni never cries.

25
00:01:23,185 --> 00:01:24,347
You like him that much?

26
00:01:30,105 --> 00:01:31,423
Please give us your approval, Mother.

27
00:01:32,465 --> 00:01:33,912
I've waited so long for this.

28
00:01:53,685 --> 00:01:56,727
These days, Mother, restaurants close
if you arrive a little late for dinner.

29
00:01:56,729 --> 00:01:58,150
It's okay.

30
00:01:58,585 --> 00:02:01,399
I'll book the restaurant
Ji Ni, her dad, and I used to go to,

31
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,520
and treat you there. It's a nice place.

32
00:02:04,752 --> 00:02:07,142
I wish Ji Ni's dad were here to see this.

33
00:02:10,545 --> 00:02:14,164
You have such beautiful, expressive eyes.

34
00:02:14,278 --> 00:02:15,678
Just like Ji Ni's dad.

35
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:17,948
He's way more handsome than dad!

36
00:02:17,979 --> 00:02:19,547
What are you talking about?

37
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:24,167
Your dad would be heartbroken
if he heard you say that.

38
00:02:24,398 --> 00:02:25,929
Thank you for the compliment.

39
00:02:26,258 --> 00:02:27,711
You're really beautiful too, Mother.

40
00:02:28,005 --> 00:02:29,238
People must think you're sisters.

41
00:02:29,239 --> 00:02:31,207
Yes, I hear that sometimes.

42
00:02:31,432 --> 00:02:34,950
I cried so much after having her
that I lost all the water in my body.

43
00:02:35,005 --> 00:02:36,385
That's why I never age.

44
00:02:36,552 --> 00:02:38,919
You need water in your body to get old.

45
00:02:39,243 --> 00:02:40,243
Yeah...

46
00:02:40,258 --> 00:02:42,565
What's with the "Yeah?"
That's complete nonsense!

47
00:02:42,691 --> 00:02:44,273
You should act your age.

48
00:02:44,938 --> 00:02:47,317
When dad was alive, mom acted like a kid.

49
00:02:47,356 --> 00:02:49,203
She always did whatever she wanted.

50
00:02:49,464 --> 00:02:51,606
She was the queen of the house.

51
00:02:52,545 --> 00:02:56,319
- I was...
- A princess. A rebellious princess.

52
00:02:58,698 --> 00:03:00,018
Have a sandwich.

53
00:03:07,558 --> 00:03:10,158
I used to envy Yeong Ju
for having two sons,

54
00:03:10,562 --> 00:03:12,158
but now I don't envy anyone anymore.

55
00:03:20,005 --> 00:03:21,005
Honey.

56
00:03:21,222 --> 00:03:24,125
Looks like we've got a son-in-law.

57
00:03:26,031 --> 00:03:28,819
He's tall, and he has such beautiful eyes.

58
00:03:29,098 --> 00:03:30,375
You saw him earlier, right?

59
00:03:32,651 --> 00:03:34,618
If they want to be together,
what can we do?

60
00:03:35,865 --> 00:03:37,435
Since things have turned out this way,

61
00:03:37,566 --> 00:03:41,537
I'm going to be the coolest mother-in-law
in the world.

62
00:03:41,734 --> 00:03:43,021
A devoted mother-in-law.

63
00:04:42,958 --> 00:04:45,048
Yes. Did you get home safely?

64
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:49,337
Tae O is treating you well, right?

65
00:04:50,845 --> 00:04:53,329
I just hope the trial ends soon
so you can go home.

66
00:04:54,082 --> 00:04:55,181
My mom?

67
00:04:56,711 --> 00:04:58,509
She didn't say anything in particular.

68
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:01,150
That's a relief.

69
00:05:01,632 --> 00:05:04,127
I was worried she might've said
she didn't approve of me.

70
00:05:05,311 --> 00:05:07,370
My mom doesn't change her mind like that.

71
00:05:07,372 --> 00:05:08,483
I can see that.

72
00:05:09,072 --> 00:05:11,921
I heard she was known for being
pretty decisive as a musician too.

73
00:05:12,725 --> 00:05:14,098
She certainly is decisive.

74
00:05:14,644 --> 00:05:15,644
Thank you.

75
00:05:15,878 --> 00:05:17,769
For being born to a great mother-in-law.

76
00:05:18,661 --> 00:05:21,965
- I'll do my best too.
- But are we married already?

77
00:05:22,731 --> 00:05:24,877
Why are you two getting so far
ahead of yourselves?

78
00:05:26,844 --> 00:05:27,844
You're right.

79
00:05:29,072 --> 00:05:31,821
I've lived as if I had no family,
even though I did.

80
00:05:32,159 --> 00:05:35,408
Meeting you and your mom
got me a little carried away.

81
00:05:36,909 --> 00:05:39,856
- What are you doing tomorrow?
- I'd like to visit O Reum,

82
00:05:39,941 --> 00:05:41,577
but I'm not sure if I can.

83
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:43,230
Yeah.

84
00:05:44,388 --> 00:05:45,388
Okay.

85
00:05:52,418 --> 00:05:55,560
Dad, mom likes Ji Hu.

86
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:57,835
Do you like him too?

87
00:06:14,945 --> 00:06:18,565
Hey! My goodness!

88
00:06:19,358 --> 00:06:21,198
What's all this?

89
00:06:21,265 --> 00:06:24,705
You're going to England soon.
How will you take all this with you?

90
00:06:24,758 --> 00:06:25,758
And...

91
00:06:26,084 --> 00:06:28,687
you asked to borrow my card.
Why did you spend so much?

92
00:06:32,938 --> 00:06:34,842
This is what I charged to your card.

93
00:06:34,858 --> 00:06:37,650
I'm keeping proof
that you bought my wedding gifts.

94
00:06:37,805 --> 00:06:39,018
Proof of a common-law marriage.

95
00:06:39,152 --> 00:06:40,152
What?

96
00:06:40,825 --> 00:06:43,902
So all this is evidence for the trial?

97
00:06:44,555 --> 00:06:45,919
Of course.

98
00:06:46,245 --> 00:06:49,350
I'm not letting Na Ji Ni
set foot in this house.

99
00:06:51,771 --> 00:06:53,719
Where does Ji Hu say he's staying?

100
00:06:54,025 --> 00:06:55,229
At Tae O's place?

101
00:06:55,649 --> 00:06:56,854
I guess so.

102
00:06:58,098 --> 00:07:00,825
I feel like I can't breathe
when I can't see my son.

103
00:07:00,892 --> 00:07:02,402
Seriously, Mother.

104
00:07:02,805 --> 00:07:04,365
What will you do when we move to England?

105
00:07:04,366 --> 00:07:05,986
At least then, I'll feel better.

106
00:07:06,071 --> 00:07:07,537
But that's not happening yet.

107
00:07:07,925 --> 00:07:09,206
I'm worried Ji Ni and her mom...

108
00:07:09,275 --> 00:07:12,418
will brainwash my innocent son.
Who knows what they'll do?

109
00:07:12,419 --> 00:07:14,667
You worry about everything.

110
00:07:17,632 --> 00:07:18,692
Mother.

111
00:07:20,552 --> 00:07:22,321
Here! What do you think?

112
00:07:25,371 --> 00:07:27,311
You bought me this last time.

113
00:07:27,313 --> 00:07:28,313
I did?

114
00:07:31,887 --> 00:07:33,506
Right!

115
00:07:33,658 --> 00:07:35,085
You little...

116
00:07:35,126 --> 00:07:38,065
How could you forget
buying something this expensive?

117
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:39,521
Right.

118
00:07:44,305 --> 00:07:45,423
Excuse me a moment.

119
00:07:47,978 --> 00:07:49,152
Yes, Counselor.

120
00:07:50,849 --> 00:07:51,849
Yes.

121
00:08:01,452 --> 00:08:02,621
So,

122
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:05,433
you're saying there's not enough evidence?

123
00:08:05,471 --> 00:08:08,033
All the evidence you sent
is from ages ago.

124
00:08:08,318 --> 00:08:10,025
My paralegal checked the dates.

125
00:08:10,058 --> 00:08:12,478
And those friends you mentioned
in England are from way back too.

126
00:08:12,885 --> 00:08:15,521
Besides the delivery orders
and your mother-in-law's recording,

127
00:08:15,645 --> 00:08:18,143
find a recording that shows
Im Ji Hu's own intent.

128
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:20,569
Okay.

129
00:08:21,812 --> 00:08:24,358
I told you, if you can't prove
you both agreed to register the marriage,

130
00:08:24,475 --> 00:08:27,057
you need to prove
you were in a common-law marriage.

131
00:08:27,085 --> 00:08:30,303
That's exactly what
I'm working so hard to prove.

132
00:08:30,305 --> 00:08:32,246
Im Ji Hu changed his registered address.

133
00:08:32,385 --> 00:08:34,423
Deliveries to that address
won't mean anything now.

134
00:08:34,424 --> 00:08:35,424
Seriously?

135
00:08:35,990 --> 00:08:37,092
Where did he move?

136
00:08:37,654 --> 00:08:38,958
Is it Seo Chon, by any chance?

137
00:08:38,971 --> 00:08:40,364
No. Cheong Du Dong.

138
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:43,912
You said you had a recording of him
agreeing to the marriage registration.

139
00:08:44,158 --> 00:08:47,137
That alone would settle everything.
Why haven't you sent it yet?

140
00:08:47,432 --> 00:08:49,718
- Do you even have it?
- I said I understand!

141
00:08:49,852 --> 00:08:51,535
I'll send it, so just wait.

142
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:53,385
Why are you treating me like a fraud?

143
00:09:02,331 --> 00:09:03,448
This is Do Do Hee.

144
00:09:04,395 --> 00:09:06,475
When will you finish
editing the recording?

145
00:09:06,631 --> 00:09:08,912
What? I said it's urgent!

146
00:09:09,502 --> 00:09:10,681
Is it done?

147
00:09:11,998 --> 00:09:13,173
You made it sound natural, right?

148
00:09:14,192 --> 00:09:16,283
Set the file date to the day
before the marriage registration too.

149
00:09:16,804 --> 00:09:19,450
- Yes.
- AI is so convincing these days.

150
00:09:19,452 --> 00:09:21,205
As long as there's no original file,
they won't catch us.

151
00:09:21,266 --> 00:09:23,487
Don't worry. I'm sending the email now.

152
00:09:29,225 --> 00:09:30,369
What a relief.

153
00:09:32,472 --> 00:09:33,587
Yes?

154
00:09:37,185 --> 00:09:38,883
We need to talk. Come downstairs.

155
00:09:56,065 --> 00:09:57,065
What...

156
00:09:57,959 --> 00:09:59,544
What do you mean by that?

157
00:10:01,085 --> 00:10:02,277
You want me to leave?

158
00:10:02,585 --> 00:10:03,769
Why all of a sudden?

159
00:10:04,765 --> 00:10:06,451
We can win the annulment case.

160
00:10:06,591 --> 00:10:08,271
You were on my side.

161
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:09,785
Weren't you?

162
00:10:10,952 --> 00:10:12,471
You two aren't in love.

163
00:10:12,552 --> 00:10:14,084
But I love him.

164
00:10:14,086 --> 00:10:15,198
Ji Hu doesn't love you.

165
00:10:15,371 --> 00:10:16,529
I've heard about it too.

166
00:10:16,531 --> 00:10:18,758
Because of you
and your mom's fake credentials,

167
00:10:18,874 --> 00:10:20,383
you're using Ji Hu.

168
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:24,077
- Father.
- I told Ambassador Do too.

169
00:10:24,145 --> 00:10:25,360
You need to give up now.

170
00:10:26,848 --> 00:10:29,294
You told my dad?

171
00:10:29,761 --> 00:10:32,227
- Yes.
- How could you tell him that?

172
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:33,299
Why?

173
00:10:35,958 --> 00:10:38,912
What do I do?

174
00:10:40,230 --> 00:10:41,504
What did my dad say?

175
00:10:41,968 --> 00:10:43,919
He said he understood. Don't worry.

176
00:10:43,985 --> 00:10:45,533
Where you studied doesn't always matter.

177
00:10:45,594 --> 00:10:48,411
No! That's not how my dad sees it!

178
00:10:50,445 --> 00:10:51,445
Do Hee.

179
00:10:51,779 --> 00:10:52,900
What's wrong with you?

180
00:10:53,054 --> 00:10:54,683
Why are you yelling? What's wrong?

181
00:10:55,578 --> 00:10:56,685
Mother.

182
00:10:56,982 --> 00:10:59,569
I need this marriage to happen. Please.

183
00:11:00,072 --> 00:11:01,727
I have nowhere to go now.

184
00:11:02,685 --> 00:11:05,573
Now that my dad knows, I'm finished.

185
00:11:08,245 --> 00:11:09,245
Father.

186
00:11:09,390 --> 00:11:10,979
Please don't abandon me.

187
00:11:11,495 --> 00:11:12,495
Please?

188
00:11:15,672 --> 00:11:17,010
What am I going to do now?

189
00:11:18,749 --> 00:11:20,279
What do I do now?

190
00:11:30,617 --> 00:11:33,217
What did they put her through...

191
00:11:33,259 --> 00:11:35,117
to make her shake like that?

192
00:11:35,845 --> 00:11:38,225
That family must've been a mess.

193
00:11:39,132 --> 00:11:40,283
You know that story, right?

194
00:11:40,545 --> 00:11:43,116
One of the guys I served with
nearly killed his son over enlistment.

195
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:44,458
Right, that family.

196
00:11:44,858 --> 00:11:46,769
I really thought it would end in tragedy.

197
00:11:46,771 --> 00:11:48,240
There are lots of strange families.

198
00:11:48,638 --> 00:11:50,227
Still, that's too much.

199
00:11:50,672 --> 00:11:51,846
But...

200
00:11:52,467 --> 00:11:55,131
why did you tell Do Hee to leave?

201
00:11:55,612 --> 00:11:58,469
Don't tell me you've been won over
to Ji Ni's side.

202
00:11:58,470 --> 00:11:59,723
Ji Hu likes her.

203
00:11:59,732 --> 00:12:00,858
Let's give in.

204
00:12:01,258 --> 00:12:04,081
- I've changed my mind.
- No. I can't.

205
00:12:05,038 --> 00:12:07,260
How can I be in-laws with that woman?

206
00:12:07,322 --> 00:12:11,158
She's a mistress.
She broke up someone else's family.

207
00:12:11,852 --> 00:12:13,992
And Na Ji Ni is proof of that crime.

208
00:12:14,098 --> 00:12:16,951
Doesn't that disgust you?
I hate even thinking about it.

209
00:12:17,005 --> 00:12:18,540
All lives are equally valuable.

210
00:12:18,665 --> 00:12:21,594
Whether you raise your biological child
or an abandoned one, it's the same.

211
00:12:21,958 --> 00:12:25,084
If you keep this up, you could lose him.
Are you okay with that?

212
00:12:25,085 --> 00:12:26,837
He's still my son, no matter what.

213
00:12:27,285 --> 00:12:30,235
I'll accept not seeing him for a while.

214
00:12:30,245 --> 00:12:32,938
It might not be just a while.
Think carefully.

215
00:12:32,939 --> 00:12:35,102
A hundred years won't change my mind.

216
00:12:35,638 --> 00:12:37,792
You're the one who needs to stand firm.

217
00:12:38,277 --> 00:12:39,824
Anyway,

218
00:12:40,225 --> 00:12:42,067
what are we going to do about poor Do Hee?

219
00:12:42,398 --> 00:12:43,983
Why does that school matter so much?

220
00:12:45,575 --> 00:12:46,575
Honestly...

221
00:13:14,529 --> 00:13:16,058
Wait!

222
00:13:18,925 --> 00:13:20,371
You're going to visit O Reum, right?

223
00:13:20,415 --> 00:13:21,654
Take this.

224
00:13:21,911 --> 00:13:22,911
What is it?

225
00:13:23,452 --> 00:13:25,227
Some yogurt drinks and rice balls.

226
00:13:25,325 --> 00:13:28,331
I remembered O Reum could only eat
rice porridge while sick.

227
00:13:28,605 --> 00:13:30,969
O Reum must've craved so many other foods.

228
00:13:31,152 --> 00:13:32,727
It broke my heart. Such a little child.

229
00:13:33,372 --> 00:13:34,372
Thank you.

230
00:13:34,373 --> 00:13:35,987
That's what family does.

231
00:13:36,558 --> 00:13:38,031
I have a lot to thank you for too.

232
00:13:38,098 --> 00:13:42,123
You went to the hospital with Ji Ni
at night. It meant a lot.

233
00:13:42,398 --> 00:13:43,814
I should've told you sooner.

234
00:13:44,314 --> 00:13:45,314
Okay.

235
00:13:45,775 --> 00:13:48,317
I talked to your mom.

236
00:13:48,325 --> 00:13:50,083
We hope you find Mai.

237
00:13:50,458 --> 00:13:53,037
When you find her, bring her home.

238
00:13:53,618 --> 00:13:57,504
Tell her not to feel embarrassed.
She should come home. Okay?

239
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,467
- Okay.
- Good.

240
00:14:05,451 --> 00:14:07,165
Would it be okay if I came too?

241
00:14:08,405 --> 00:14:10,185
I miss O Reum.

242
00:14:10,719 --> 00:14:11,719
Of course.

243
00:14:12,222 --> 00:14:13,417
Thank you.

244
00:14:16,298 --> 00:14:17,396
Have a good visit.

245
00:14:21,824 --> 00:14:22,845
Hello.

246
00:14:26,184 --> 00:14:28,096
- Ji Hu.
- Ji Ni told me...

247
00:14:28,132 --> 00:14:30,339
you two were going to visit O Reum today,

248
00:14:30,656 --> 00:14:32,332
so I wondered if I could join you.

249
00:14:33,012 --> 00:14:35,160
If you'd rather I didn't,
I'll just give you the flowers.

250
00:14:36,848 --> 00:14:39,759
- Well...
- What perfect timing to join us.

251
00:14:39,952 --> 00:14:42,702
Am I the only one
who thinks he's a bit like Sa Bin?

252
00:14:43,025 --> 00:14:44,025
Actually...

253
00:14:44,109 --> 00:14:46,423
O Reum is the reason we met.

254
00:14:47,165 --> 00:14:48,572
- At the hospital...
- Okay.

255
00:14:48,732 --> 00:14:49,732
Let's all go together.

256
00:14:51,054 --> 00:14:54,096
O Reum will be so excited
to have this many visitors.

257
00:14:56,624 --> 00:14:57,775
Ji Hu.

258
00:15:01,432 --> 00:15:02,954
I miss O Reum too.

259
00:15:04,817 --> 00:15:05,817
Let's go.

260
00:15:17,991 --> 00:15:19,429
Enjoy the food, O Reum.

261
00:15:20,827 --> 00:15:23,070
Hello, O Reum. Long time no see.

262
00:15:28,418 --> 00:15:29,550
Hello, O Reum.

263
00:15:34,678 --> 00:15:35,816
This...

264
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:38,066
Doesn't this mean Mai was here?

265
00:15:40,345 --> 00:15:41,418
It seems so.

266
00:15:47,052 --> 00:15:49,360
Did you know? You seem so calm.

267
00:15:49,385 --> 00:15:51,027
She's his mom. Of course she'd come.

268
00:15:55,322 --> 00:15:56,322
Ji Ni.

269
00:15:56,537 --> 00:15:57,537
Ji Hu.

270
00:16:14,477 --> 00:16:16,187
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

271
00:16:16,212 --> 00:16:18,236
I just have such an amazing husband.

272
00:16:18,555 --> 00:16:20,842
O Reum will grow up to have...

273
00:16:20,866 --> 00:16:22,655
a heart as big as yours, right?

274
00:16:29,991 --> 00:16:31,041
O Reum.

275
00:16:31,294 --> 00:16:32,294
(The late Cha O Reum)

276
00:16:32,328 --> 00:16:33,745
I'll come see you again.

277
00:16:43,591 --> 00:16:46,190
You want Ji Hu to stay at my house?

278
00:16:46,261 --> 00:16:48,067
What? No...

279
00:16:48,494 --> 00:16:51,026
I live there, so it's my house now.

280
00:16:51,705 --> 00:16:53,870
You're crossing the line again.

281
00:16:56,618 --> 00:17:00,230
No. They're already worried
about him going to Ji Ni.

282
00:17:00,254 --> 00:17:03,281
His parents are keeping
a close eye on him.

283
00:17:03,298 --> 00:17:05,230
That's why I want him at our place.

284
00:17:05,263 --> 00:17:07,127
Do Hee has the marriage papers.

285
00:17:07,152 --> 00:17:08,637
Those papers scare me.

286
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:12,467
They can object all they want.
Ji Hu is my daughter's man.

287
00:17:12,492 --> 00:17:14,579
I'm going to make that clear.

288
00:17:14,604 --> 00:17:17,199
My sons are there too.
It'll be awkward for everyone.

289
00:17:17,224 --> 00:17:19,389
You said the trial would take a few days.

290
00:17:19,414 --> 00:17:22,826
He's so tall. How can we let him
sleep uncomfortably on a couch?

291
00:17:22,851 --> 00:17:25,281
You really adore your son-in-law now.

292
00:17:25,472 --> 00:17:27,844
Of course! He's my daughter's man.

293
00:17:27,868 --> 00:17:29,600
Don't overdo it.

294
00:17:30,598 --> 00:17:31,893
Actually...

295
00:17:32,390 --> 00:17:35,320
I locked Ji Ni in her room...

296
00:17:35,344 --> 00:17:37,487
and pushed her to go on matchmaking dates.

297
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:41,506
But they were all illegitimate sons
of wealthy families.

298
00:17:41,684 --> 00:17:44,562
Like she had to marry someone like her.

299
00:17:45,198 --> 00:17:48,070
It's my fault,
but Ji Ni gets blamed for it.

300
00:17:48,973 --> 00:17:50,237
Yeong Ju.

301
00:17:50,509 --> 00:17:53,069
Ji Ni won't end up like me, right?

302
00:17:53,070 --> 00:17:54,576
Of course not.

303
00:17:54,618 --> 00:17:56,583
Will my sons end up like their dad?

304
00:17:56,851 --> 00:17:58,839
They make their own choices.

305
00:18:00,398 --> 00:18:03,096
Anyway, I'm having Ji Hu come over.

306
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,120
Okay?

307
00:18:04,177 --> 00:18:06,308
Why are you in such a hurry?

308
00:18:06,516 --> 00:18:10,503
I'd better go put Ji Hu on a leash.

309
00:18:12,652 --> 00:18:13,652
By the way,

310
00:18:14,188 --> 00:18:16,518
is this Ji Hu's mom's shop?

311
00:18:16,621 --> 00:18:18,414
Yes. Why?

312
00:18:21,072 --> 00:18:23,244
She's really overworking you.

313
00:18:23,505 --> 00:18:24,823
Make sure you're getting paid.

314
00:18:25,552 --> 00:18:27,109
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

315
00:18:34,418 --> 00:18:35,686
Yes, Seung Hyun? What is it?

316
00:18:35,711 --> 00:18:38,670
Seung Woo was filming in the mountains...

317
00:18:38,798 --> 00:18:40,931
- and his prosthetic leg broke.
- The mountains?

318
00:18:41,852 --> 00:18:43,342
Is he out of his mind?

319
00:18:44,872 --> 00:18:46,796
Okay. I'll head to the hospital too.

320
00:18:48,609 --> 00:18:50,222
Unbelievable.

321
00:18:54,765 --> 00:18:57,330
- Ji Hu.
- Mother.

322
00:19:02,265 --> 00:19:04,995
What a sweet boy.

323
00:19:05,675 --> 00:19:07,782
Come to Seo Chon after work.

324
00:19:07,807 --> 00:19:10,539
- Don't settle for your friend's couch.
- It's okay. I'm fine.

325
00:19:10,789 --> 00:19:13,929
- Her brothers are there too.
- Don't feel awkward. It's our house.

326
00:19:13,953 --> 00:19:15,473
It's Ji Ni's dad's house.

327
00:19:15,793 --> 00:19:17,099
Okay.

328
00:19:17,124 --> 00:19:20,353
Don't think you can disrespect us
just because we're two women,

329
00:19:20,377 --> 00:19:21,983
or you'll regret it.

330
00:19:22,008 --> 00:19:23,483
Of course not.

331
00:19:23,592 --> 00:19:24,926
I would never do that.

332
00:19:25,812 --> 00:19:29,349
Ji Ni's dad has passed away,
but she still has her brothers and me,

333
00:19:29,373 --> 00:19:31,348
so stay on your toes. Got it?

334
00:19:31,731 --> 00:19:32,731
Okay.

335
00:19:33,368 --> 00:19:34,595
How cute.

336
00:19:36,911 --> 00:19:40,406
Her dad had such sweet eyes too,
just like yours.

337
00:19:41,588 --> 00:19:42,588
Yes...

338
00:19:44,031 --> 00:19:45,914
Work hard,

339
00:19:45,938 --> 00:19:47,498
then come right home.

340
00:19:47,523 --> 00:19:49,307
Don't even look at anyone else.

341
00:19:49,404 --> 00:19:51,769
I'll time how long it takes you
to get from here to the house.

342
00:19:51,794 --> 00:19:53,534
And from now on,

343
00:19:53,564 --> 00:19:57,514
whenever you make plans without Ji Ni,
make sure you tell me. Okay?

344
00:19:58,051 --> 00:19:59,460
- Yes.
- Yeah.

345
00:20:29,771 --> 00:20:30,771
Who are you?

346
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:33,685
She has a daughter?

347
00:20:33,945 --> 00:20:36,021
I met your mom before.

348
00:20:36,458 --> 00:20:39,248
So the one who got into the accident
was your older brother?

349
00:20:39,458 --> 00:20:40,552
Or the younger one?

350
00:20:40,812 --> 00:20:41,968
The accident?

351
00:20:41,993 --> 00:20:44,799
The motorcycle accident
when you were kids.

352
00:20:44,823 --> 00:20:46,758
Are you a witness?

353
00:20:47,183 --> 00:20:49,964
Your mom said the case was closed.

354
00:20:49,988 --> 00:20:51,373
My mom told you that?

355
00:20:54,252 --> 00:20:55,735
But what brings you here?

356
00:20:58,692 --> 00:21:00,431
I moved back to this neighborhood.

357
00:21:00,456 --> 00:21:02,824
I opened a rice cake shop
at the entrance to the alley.

358
00:21:02,885 --> 00:21:04,089
I wanted you to try these.

359
00:21:04,437 --> 00:21:06,021
Okay.

360
00:21:06,905 --> 00:21:08,255
Thank you.

361
00:21:26,732 --> 00:21:28,552
- Mom.
- I'm in a meeting.

362
00:21:28,576 --> 00:21:29,913
I'll call you later.

363
00:21:31,476 --> 00:21:32,723
Seriously!

364
00:21:38,338 --> 00:21:39,589
Are you okay?

365
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,373
Mom, just go.

366
00:21:42,399 --> 00:21:44,020
I'm telling you, I'm fine!

367
00:21:44,028 --> 00:21:45,955
Stop making such a fuss. Am I a child?

368
00:21:45,997 --> 00:21:47,702
If you're not a child,
why are you so reckless?

369
00:21:48,054 --> 00:21:49,393
Why hike with that leg?

370
00:21:49,888 --> 00:21:52,556
It wasn't a hike.
I just didn't watch where I was going.

371
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:54,702
That prosthetic leg is the problem.

372
00:21:54,852 --> 00:21:56,654
It's ridiculously expensive
and keeps breaking.

373
00:21:56,679 --> 00:21:58,414
It's time to replace it.

374
00:21:58,439 --> 00:22:00,253
I told you to replace it,
but you said it was fine.

375
00:22:00,278 --> 00:22:03,018
Anyway, I'll handle it myself.
Stop worrying...

376
00:22:03,265 --> 00:22:05,095
and mind your own business.

377
00:22:06,285 --> 00:22:07,854
You're always so temperamental!

378
00:22:09,249 --> 00:22:11,227
Leave him alone. He's upset.

379
00:22:12,065 --> 00:22:13,170
Are you going to the shop?

380
00:22:13,315 --> 00:22:14,315
Of course.

381
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:15,785
You should go too, Mom.

382
00:22:15,810 --> 00:22:16,810
Go on.

383
00:22:27,105 --> 00:22:30,341
Ma'am, they still haven't caught
the hit-and-run driver, have they?

384
00:22:30,494 --> 00:22:33,231
I wish I could grab them by the collar
and shake them.

385
00:22:33,905 --> 00:22:36,021
Every time I see him like this,
it breaks my heart.

386
00:22:36,771 --> 00:22:39,258
How could someone ruin
a perfectly healthy child's leg like that,

387
00:22:39,498 --> 00:22:41,713
then spend their whole life on the run?

388
00:22:45,219 --> 00:22:47,179
Ji Hu.

389
00:22:47,576 --> 00:22:49,950
You heard he's coming here today, right?

390
00:22:50,630 --> 00:22:51,630
Yes.

391
00:22:51,931 --> 00:22:53,365
Are you okay with that?

392
00:22:53,390 --> 00:22:55,355
It's only for a few days.

393
00:22:55,692 --> 00:22:57,321
The trial's coming up anyway.

394
00:22:57,792 --> 00:23:00,938
Your mom wants her son-in-law close by.

395
00:23:02,445 --> 00:23:05,327
Living under one roof helps you bond.
Look at you.

396
00:23:05,352 --> 00:23:06,846
You're getting close to my kids too,

397
00:23:06,870 --> 00:23:08,362
one way or another.

398
00:23:09,018 --> 00:23:11,336
I'm really grateful.

399
00:23:12,484 --> 00:23:14,510
I think your mom held on this long...

400
00:23:14,674 --> 00:23:17,549
so you'd have blood relatives.

401
00:23:18,192 --> 00:23:21,737
We adults, ended up living like enemies,

402
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:24,909
but you three are still blood relatives.

403
00:23:26,266 --> 00:23:27,266
Blood relatives.

404
00:23:28,382 --> 00:23:29,864
What does that even mean?

405
00:23:30,815 --> 00:23:32,098
I wonder.

406
00:23:33,548 --> 00:23:34,548
I'll get going.

407
00:23:34,811 --> 00:23:35,811
Okay.

408
00:23:51,085 --> 00:23:52,085
Mom!

409
00:23:52,408 --> 00:23:53,654
You scared me!

410
00:23:53,785 --> 00:23:54,785
What?

411
00:23:58,752 --> 00:23:59,752
Mom, what's going on?

412
00:23:59,976 --> 00:24:02,367
Why did you lie and say
the hit-and-run case was closed?

413
00:24:02,678 --> 00:24:03,991
How did you find that out?

414
00:24:04,015 --> 00:24:05,412
A witness came by.

415
00:24:05,437 --> 00:24:07,799
My heart was pounding like crazy earlier.

416
00:24:08,104 --> 00:24:10,260
Yeong Ju left in tears again today.

417
00:24:10,285 --> 00:24:12,330
He got hurt while filming
and came in on crutches.

418
00:24:12,355 --> 00:24:14,083
Imagine how heartbreaking that must be.

419
00:24:14,770 --> 00:24:15,976
Why did you do it?

420
00:24:16,212 --> 00:24:19,067
Why did that woman come back here again?

421
00:24:19,092 --> 00:24:20,837
She moved back to this neighborhood.

422
00:24:21,098 --> 00:24:23,004
She brought rice cakes
because she opened a shop nearby.

423
00:24:23,028 --> 00:24:24,198
She came back?

424
00:24:24,565 --> 00:24:27,644
I couldn't tell Yeong Ju,
so I froze the rice cakes.

425
00:24:29,458 --> 00:24:30,889
Tell me what really happened. Hurry.

426
00:24:30,913 --> 00:24:31,913
What?

427
00:24:33,410 --> 00:24:35,977
She's a con artist. Can't you tell?

428
00:24:36,092 --> 00:24:37,339
What are you talking about?

429
00:24:37,479 --> 00:24:41,193
She came by a long time ago. When was it?

430
00:24:41,218 --> 00:24:44,198
When Mai ran away from home
and everything was in chaos.

431
00:24:44,222 --> 00:24:46,338
- That's when she showed up.
- So?

432
00:24:46,363 --> 00:24:50,338
I took her to a nearby cafe
and questioned her about everything.

433
00:24:50,363 --> 00:24:52,612
She couldn't give me
a straight answer to anything.

434
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:55,305
It was all lies.

435
00:24:55,330 --> 00:24:58,698
Since Seung Hyun offered a reward
for finding the witness,

436
00:24:58,722 --> 00:25:01,022
she came to collect the money.

437
00:25:01,071 --> 00:25:03,418
So I told her the case was closed.

438
00:25:03,545 --> 00:25:06,295
- Is that true?
- Who are you accusing of lying?

439
00:25:06,320 --> 00:25:08,473
What would I gain by lying about that?

440
00:25:08,596 --> 00:25:10,488
Besides, Seung Hyun said it himself.

441
00:25:10,490 --> 00:25:13,863
Lots of people make up stories
just to collect the reward.

442
00:25:14,978 --> 00:25:16,211
You're telling the truth, right?

443
00:25:16,274 --> 00:25:18,898
Have you been lied to your whole life?

444
00:25:20,091 --> 00:25:22,721
When is Ji Hu coming?

445
00:25:23,345 --> 00:25:25,525
I don't know.
I was so shaken up earlier...

446
00:25:25,550 --> 00:25:27,149
I thought I was going to die.

447
00:25:27,209 --> 00:25:28,703
What are you talking about?

448
00:25:28,740 --> 00:25:31,115
Why were you so shaken up?

449
00:25:31,580 --> 00:25:34,006
What were you thinking, Na Ji Ni?

450
00:25:34,761 --> 00:25:37,014
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

451
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:39,153
You little brat. Seriously!

452
00:25:39,253 --> 00:25:40,253
It's Ji Hu.

453
00:25:40,416 --> 00:25:43,840
I'm still mad at you.
We'll finish this later.

454
00:25:43,874 --> 00:25:46,002
Okay. I said I'm sorry.

455
00:25:56,601 --> 00:25:59,734
Why on earth did that woman come back?

456
00:26:02,193 --> 00:26:03,734
My hands are really shaking.

457
00:26:05,686 --> 00:26:06,686
Ji Hu.

458
00:26:07,531 --> 00:26:08,682
Yes, Counselor.

459
00:26:10,126 --> 00:26:11,126
What?

460
00:26:11,150 --> 00:26:12,281
A recording?

461
00:26:13,031 --> 00:26:14,298
The other side submitted a recording...

462
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:16,823
as evidence of you asking her
to register your marriage.

463
00:26:16,971 --> 00:26:19,307
Mr. Im Ji Hu,
we can't get this annulled now.

464
00:26:19,332 --> 00:26:20,686
We won't win the case.

465
00:26:20,711 --> 00:26:22,911
We need to switch to a divorce suit now.

466
00:26:22,936 --> 00:26:24,702
No. That can't be right.

467
00:26:25,447 --> 00:26:28,011
I'll look into it.
Please send me the recording now.

468
00:26:28,507 --> 00:26:29,507
Okay.

469
00:26:31,433 --> 00:26:33,694
What does he mean? What recording?

470
00:26:34,542 --> 00:26:35,748
I don't know either.

471
00:26:41,660 --> 00:26:44,440
Ji Hu, your mom picked our wedding venue.

472
00:26:44,560 --> 00:26:47,159
Now that we have a date,
I'll send out digital invitations.

473
00:26:47,239 --> 00:26:49,315
- And let's register our marriage.
- Register our marriage?

474
00:26:49,340 --> 00:26:51,603
Yeah, your mom says we should too.

475
00:26:51,628 --> 00:26:53,284
I'm so happy.

476
00:26:53,308 --> 00:26:55,529
Okay, let's do that. I'll call you later.

477
00:26:55,796 --> 00:26:58,248
Ji Hu, don't change your mind.

478
00:26:58,362 --> 00:27:01,961
Remember, you're all I have.

479
00:27:02,370 --> 00:27:03,570
Don't worry.

480
00:27:06,193 --> 00:27:08,284
That sounds like you.

481
00:27:09,571 --> 00:27:11,215
No, that's not me.

482
00:27:11,333 --> 00:27:14,093
Ji Ni, please believe me.
I never said that.

483
00:27:15,373 --> 00:27:16,954
Then what is this?

484
00:27:18,121 --> 00:27:19,584
I don't know.

485
00:27:20,244 --> 00:27:21,244
But...

486
00:27:21,438 --> 00:27:23,098
I clearly remember this conversation.

487
00:27:23,759 --> 00:27:24,903
The evening before,

488
00:27:24,927 --> 00:27:27,003
I got my memory back
while playing piano with you,

489
00:27:27,483 --> 00:27:29,875
and we went to the Han River.
This was the next day.

490
00:27:30,088 --> 00:27:33,236
Do Hee said this,
and I told her not to do anything.

491
00:27:33,583 --> 00:27:35,783
I'm sure we were supposed to meet
at the publishing house later.

492
00:27:36,087 --> 00:27:37,087
But...

493
00:27:37,583 --> 00:27:39,893
how could it have been recorded like this?

494
00:27:40,610 --> 00:27:42,300
I don't know.

495
00:27:47,046 --> 00:27:48,712
So this is where you've been.

496
00:27:52,433 --> 00:27:54,314
How could you do this to me?

497
00:27:54,812 --> 00:27:56,973
How could you tell your dad
all my secrets?

498
00:27:57,627 --> 00:27:59,875
You know better than anyone
what'll happen to me!

499
00:28:01,218 --> 00:28:03,026
Did you think I'd just die like this?

500
00:28:03,461 --> 00:28:04,998
Not a chance.

501
00:28:05,787 --> 00:28:07,672
I'm not going down alone.

502
00:28:39,392 --> 00:28:42,588
(Family Register)

503
00:28:42,613 --> 00:28:45,535
Ji Hu, stop letting that crazy woman
lead you around and come home!

504
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:48,075
- I'll be staying here for a few days.
- I could die happy now.

505
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:49,552
You look so happy with your brothers.

506
00:28:49,580 --> 00:28:52,126
- What's this?
- A witness to Director Cha's accident.

507
00:28:52,151 --> 00:28:53,399
Can I leave this here for a bit?

508
00:28:53,424 --> 00:28:55,555
I'm going to die before this is over.
This is killing me.

509
00:28:55,580 --> 00:28:57,385
I can win. I've got everything ready.

510
00:28:57,410 --> 00:28:58,757
We need to search Do Hee's phone.

511
00:28:58,782 --> 00:29:00,276
Think you'll find something on that phone?

512
00:29:00,301 --> 00:29:02,259
The trial's coming up soon.

513
00:29:03,159 --> 00:29:05,159
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
